        # ReleaseNotes of this module
        ReleaseNotes = 'v2.5.0 : adds Invoke-OnyphePivot, a new public cmdlet that pivots from a prior Onyphe result set to a follow-up search per distinct value of a field (e.g. take every subject.organization seen in a ctl result set and fire a follow-up query for each). Captures the useful part of the official onyphe/cli''s opp companion tool auto-pivot processors (Andlookup/Orlookup/Pivots/Whois) without porting its other 24 purely client-side formatting/filtering processors, which PowerShell''s own object pipeline (Where-Object/Group-Object/Sort-Object -Unique) already covers natively. Architecture (per explicit user sign-off via AskUserQuestion): one API call per distinct pivot value (not a single OR-combined query) - mirrors this project''s own manual OSINT technique and keeps clear provenance; two separate parameters, -PivotField (dotted source property path, e.g. "subject.organization") and -PivotFilter (target OQL filter name, e.g. "organization"), since those often differ across categories. -PivotCategory/-PivotFilter are DynamicParams validated against Get-OnypheSearchCategories/Get-OnypheSearchFilters, same pattern as Search-OnypheInfo. Every returned result is tagged with cli-pivot_source_field/cli-pivot_source_value NoteProperties recording provenance. Supports -Wait (delay between each follow-up call, useful given this can fire many calls), plus -Size/-TrackQuery/-Calculated/-UseBetaFeatures/-Post passthrough to each call. Live-tested end-to-end with a real API key (piped a small ctl result set through it, confirmed one follow-up call fired per distinct subject.organization value, results correctly tagged). 395 Pester tests (up from 386). No breaking changes - a new, separate public cmdlet. v2.4.0 : adds POST-based /search and /export support (the official onyphe/cli exposes both search/export - GET, OQL in the URL - and post_search/post_export - POST, OQL in the request body - specifically so a very long OQL string, many OR-terms/exclusions, does not hit a URL-length limit). New -Post switch on Search-OnypheInfo and Export-OnypheInfo (and their private Invoke-APIOnypheSearch/Invoke-APIOnypheExport wrappers) - when set, the OQL query is sent as a form-urlencoded POST body (field "query") instead of a GET q= query-string parameter; page/size/trackquery/calculated still go in the query string either way, matching the official CLI''s own post_search/post_request behavior (confirmed by reading Onyphe::Api.pm''s post_request/stream subs directly from the upstream repo). Invoke-OnypheAPIV2 (the core HTTP transport) gained the underlying logic: when -Method POST and -QueryValue are both set (and no -data/-file JSON body is also being sent), the query moves to a "query=<url-encoded>" POST body with Content-Type application/x-www-form-urlencoded, instead of being appended to the URL. Live-tested end-to-end against both /search and /export with a real API key - identical result counts/content between the existing GET path and the new POST path for the same query. 386 Pester tests (up from 379). No breaking changes - purely additive opt-in switch, GET behavior for existing callers is unchanged. v2.3.9 : adds the "bootstrapcertsowildcard" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Bootstrap Certso Wildcard APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/bootstrap/certso/wildcard) - seeds a wildcard-domain search from a certificate subject.organization value, discovering wildcard domain pattern(s) linked to it. Uses the "certso"-keyed request body, same shape as domaincertso/ipcertso (NOT domain-keyed despite its "wildcard" name - confirmed live: sending "domain" instead returns error 1002 "certso: parameter error: certso not given"); Get-OnypheASDInfo''s -Value-to-Certso dispatcher mapping now covers domaincertso/ipcertso/bootstrapcertsowildcard. Last of the ~21-22 stdapis endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis - only pivot/query (advapis, unlicensed on this account) remains out of scope. Live-tested with real data: "ONYPHE" returned error 1006 "search failed: no result found"; "DigiCert Inc" returned a clean success with 0 results; "Bleu SAS" returned error 1011 "too many results, you should create a task" - confirmed the astask/Wait-OnypheASDTask workflow end-to-end, but found the eventual task result was still 0 results, meaning error 1011''s size estimate does not guarantee a large final result set once computed. -AsTask is not exposed by this wrapper, same reasoning as orginventory. 379 Pester tests (up from 377). No breaking changes. v2.3.8 : adds the "websubdomaindomain" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Web Subdomain Domain APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/web/subdomain/domain) - discovers subdomain(s)/hostname(s) for one or more domains from web crawl data, returning a mix of {"hostname":"..."} entries and a trailing {"domain":"..."} echo of the query itself. Same bare "domain"-array request body as domaintld, and unlike the three "*Exist" endpoints, -IncludePattern/-ExcludePattern/-Untrusted genuinely filter server-side here (live-verified: -ExcludePattern "blog" against "onyphe.io" dropped blog.onyphe.io from the result set). Twelfth of the endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis, and second-to-last of the ~21-22 stdapis total. Live-tested with real data: "onyphe.io" returned 5 results; "sovcloud-core.fr" returned 8 real internal-looking hostnames; "sovcloud-api.fr" returned 38; "neocase-sov.fr" returned 3. A domain with a large enough footprint ("microsoft.com" in testing) can time out server-side (error 2 "request timed out") rather than fail outright, the same characteristic already seen on ipinventory - not an astask/task-mode situation like orginventory/domainexist, just a computation-time limit. A genuinely non-existent domain returns error 1006 "search failed: no result found". 377 Pester tests (up from 376). No breaking changes. v2.3.7 : adds the "domainexist" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Domain Exist APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/domain/exist) - checks whether one or more domains exist, returning {"domain":"...","exist":"true"|"false"} per domain. Same bare "domain"-array request body as dnsdomainexist/dnsdomainnsexist; does not support -IncludePattern/-ExcludePattern/-Untrusted either (not documented by Onyphe). Eleventh of the endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis, and last of the three "*Exist" endpoints. Live-tested with real data and found this one behaves differently from its two exist-type siblings: a small domain ("onyphe.io", "neocase-sov.fr") returns a clean "exist":"true" synchronously, but "sovcloud-core.fr", "sovcloud-api.fr" and "microsoft.com" all returned HTTP error 1011 "too many results, you should create a task" - the same astask/Wait-OnypheASDTask background-task mode org/inventory needs, confirmed working end-to-end (astask:"true" against sovcloud-core.fr eventually returned a normal "exist":"true" record via the task-polling path). A genuinely non-existent domain ("doesnotexist-abc123xyz.io") returned HTTP error 1006 "search failed: no result found" instead of an "exist":"false" record - the opposite of dnsdomainexist/dnsdomainnsexist''s behavior for the same case. -AsTask is not exposed by this wrapper, same reasoning as orginventory. 376 Pester tests (up from 373). No breaking changes. v2.3.6 : adds the "dnsdomainnsexist" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Dns Domain Ns Exist APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/dns/domain/ns/exist) - checks whether one or more domains have an existing NS record (a live DNS lookup), returning {"domain":"...","exist":"true"|"false"} per domain. Same bare "domain"-array request body as dnsdomainexist; like that sibling endpoint, does not support -IncludePattern/-ExcludePattern/-Untrusted (not documented by Onyphe for either endpoint). Tenth of the endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis. Live-tested with real data: "onyphe.io", "microsoft.com", "sovcloud-core.fr" and "sovcloud-api.fr" all returned exist:"true"; a deliberately made-up domain ("doesnotexist-abc123xyz.io") returned exist:"false", confirming the endpoint performs a genuine live check rather than always returning true. 373 Pester tests (up from 370). No breaking changes. v2.3.5 : adds the "dnsdomainmstenantid" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Dns Domain MsTenantId APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/dns/domain/mstenantid, a live DNS lookup) - given one or more domains, returns every OTHER domain sharing the same Microsoft 365 tenant, not the tenant ID value itself. Ninth of the endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis. Live-tested with real data: "microsoft.com" returned 107 genuinely Microsoft-owned sibling domains (xbox.com, linkedin.com, github.com, skype.com, azure.com, ...) - a domain-to-domain pivot via shared M365 tenant membership, useful for organizational footprint discovery. "onyphe.io" returned exactly 1 result (itself, no siblings found). "sovcloud-core.fr"/"sovcloud-api.fr"/"neocase-sov.fr" all returned error 1006 "no result found" - none of this project''s own tracked domains are themselves Microsoft 365 tenant domains, so despite the endpoint''s superficial "Bleu/Microsoft" naming relevance flagged in the original gap analysis, it does not actually apply to or help enumerate that domain family. 370 Pester tests (up from 369). No breaking changes. v2.3.4 : adds the "scoreinventory" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Score Inventory APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/score/inventory) - discovers risk-flagged findings for one or more domains (raw riskscan-shaped records, e.g. an expired certificate on a live host tagged "risk::certexpired"), rolled up as an attack-surface inventory. Same nested-"inventory"-object body shape as subnetinventory/ipinventory/orginventory/vhostinventory. Eighth of the endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis. Live-tested with real data: "sovcloud-core.fr" returned 13 real risk-flagged findings; "google.com" returned 1,714 results synchronously with no size-ceiling error, same as vhostinventory - the astask/Wait-OnypheASDTask workaround does not appear necessary for typical use of this endpoint either. "onyphe.io" returned error 1006 "no result found", the same per-value data gap already seen on other ASD endpoints. 369 Pester tests (up from 367). No breaking changes. v2.3.3 : adds the "vhostinventory" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Vhost Inventory APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/vhost/inventory) - discovers the virtual host(s)/forward DNS hostname(s) belonging to one or more domains, rolled up as an attack-surface inventory. Same nested-"inventory"-object body shape as subnetinventory/ipinventory/orginventory. Seventh of the 13 endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis. Live-tested with real data: "sovcloud-core.fr" returned 21 real forward hostnames; "google.com" returned 1,338 results synchronously with no size-ceiling error - unlike orginventory, this endpoint did not hit HTTP error 1011 on a large domain in testing, so the astask/Wait-OnypheASDTask workaround appears unnecessary for typical use (not exhaustively tested against every possible domain size). "onyphe.io" returned error 1006 "no result found", the same per-value data gap already seen on other ASD endpoints for that value. 367 Pester tests (up from 365). No breaking changes. v2.3.2 : adds the "ipdomain" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Ip Domain APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/ip/domain) - discovers the IP address(es) belonging to one or more domains. Same bare "domain"-array request body as domaintld (no dispatcher change needed - Get-OnypheASDInfo already maps -Value to -Domain generically for every type except the certso-keyed ones). Sixth of the 13 endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis. Live-tested with real data: "sovcloud-core.fr" returned 83 real IPs (all inside that domain''s already-known subnets); "onyphe.io" returned error 1006 "no result found", the same per-value data gap already seen on the certso endpoints for that value. Multiple domains in one call are unioned server-side. 365 Pester tests (up from 364). No breaking changes. v2.3.1 : adds the "ipcertso" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Ip Certso APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/ip/certso) - discovers the IP address(es) belonging to a certificate subject.organization value. Same "certso"-keyed request body shape as domaincertso (not the nested "inventory" object used by the *Inventory endpoints); Get-OnypheASDInfo''s dispatcher now maps -Value to -Certso for both domaincertso and ipcertso instead of just the former. Fourth of the 13 endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis. Live-tested with real data: "DigiCert Inc" returned 6,046 real IPs; "Bleu SAS" and "ONYPHE" both returned error 1006 "no result found" - same as domaincertso does for "ONYPHE" on this account, confirming this is a per-value "no matching data" result rather than an endpoint-level problem (unlike subnetinventory, where every domain tried failed the same way). 364 Pester tests (up from 361). No breaking changes. v2.3.0 : adds ASD task management - 4 new public cmdlets, Get-OnypheASDTask (v1/asd/task/id/<id>, fetch a finished task''s result), Get-OnypheASDTaskList (v1/asd/task/list, list all tasks for the account), Wait-OnypheASDTask (polls Get-OnypheASDTaskList until a task finishes, then returns its result via Get-OnypheASDTask - -PollIntervalSec/-TimeoutSec, default 5s/300s), and Stop-OnypheASDTask (v1/asd/task/kill/<id>, an HTTP DELETE - the first DELETE-method endpoint in this module, so Invoke-OnypheAPIV2''s -Method ValidateSet was extended from GET/POST to include DELETE, SupportsShouldProcess since it is destructive). Closes the practical blocker found in v2.2.6: an ASD *inventory endpoint (e.g. Get-OnypheASDInfo -ASDAPIType orginventory) that returns error 1011 "too many results, you should create a task" for a large domain can now actually be finished - resend the same call with an "astask":"true" field in its request body (confirmed live it must be the literal string "true", not a JSON boolean, unlike every other true/false field in this module) to get a .taskid back, then Wait-OnypheASDTask -TaskId <id> to retrieve the real result once ready. Live-tested the full lifecycle end-to-end: triggered a real async org/inventory task, polled it to completion, fetched its 302-organization result via Get-OnypheASDTask, and killed/cleared it via Stop-OnypheASDTask - also discovered and documented that this account allows only one task at a time (a second astask:true call fails with error 1008 until the previous task is explicitly cleared with Stop-OnypheASDTask, even after it finished) and that Get-OnypheASDTaskList returns error 1007 ("task not found: empty list") for an empty list rather than an empty success, which callers should treat as empty, not a failure. 361 Pester tests (up from 339), full doc sync. No breaking changes to existing cmdlets - Invoke-OnypheAPIV2''s new DELETE Method value is additive, GET/POST behavior unchanged. v2.2.6 : adds the "orginventory" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Org Inventory APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/org/inventory) - discovers the organization(s) associated with one or more domains, rolled up as an attack-surface inventory. Same nested-"inventory"-object body shape as v2.2.4/v2.2.5. Third of the 13 endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis. Live-tested with a partial-usability finding: the endpoint itself works correctly (small domains return a clean "success" with 0 results, not an error), but large well-known domains (google.com, github.com) return error 1011 "too many results, you should create a task" along with the real total (308,407 and 2,620,852 respectively) - the server requires the still-unimplemented ASD "astask" background-task mode (asd/task/id, /poll, /list, /kill) for results of that size, so this endpoint is not yet fully useful for any domain large enough to have real org-inventory data. Documented as a known limitation in the wrapper''s comment-based help. 339 Pester tests (up from 337). No breaking changes. v2.2.5 : adds the "ipinventory" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Ip Inventory APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/ip/inventory) - discovers the IP address(es) belonging to one or more domains, rolled up as an attack-surface inventory. Same nested-"inventory"-object request body shape as v2.2.4''s subnetinventory. Second of the 13 endpoints found missing by the onyphe/cli gap analysis. Unlike subnetinventory, **this one live-verified as fully working**: returned 519 real IPs for a domain with independently-known infrastructure, and every returned IP fell inside one of that domain''s already-confirmed subnets (cross-checked against Results/CertAndDNS/bleu_sas_subnets.csv from an earlier session) - confirms the "inventory" request shape itself is correct and the subnetinventory caveat is specific to that one endpoint, not a shared inventory-family problem. Large domains can time out server-side (error 2, "request timed out") rather than fail outright - a server-side computation-time characteristic, not a client defect. 337 Pester tests (up from 335). No breaking changes. v2.2.4 : adds the "subnetinventory" ASD API type to Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the ASD Subnet Inventory APIv1 endpoint (v1/asd/subnet/inventory) - discovers the subnet(s) belonging to one or more domains, rolled up as an attack-surface inventory. Unlike the other 9 ASD endpoints, the request body nests the input under an "inventory" object rather than a bare "domain" key, matching the shape used by Onyphe''s official onyphe/cli reference implementation. Found via a gap analysis against that CLI - the official tooling documents 22 "standard" ASD endpoints total, only 9 of which this module had implemented; this is the first of the remaining 13 to be added, chosen because it directly supports this module''s own organization/domain-family recon workflows. Live account entitlement re-confirmed via Get-OnypheUserInfo before starting: asd.stdapis is licensed on the verification account, asd.advapis (needed for the separate Pivot Query API) is not, unchanged from v2.2.0. Live-tested with a caveat: the request reaches the server and gets a genuine business-logic response (error 1006, "no result found") rather than an auth/format error, confirming the request shape is correct, but every domain tried - including microsoft.com/google.com - returned that same "no result found", unlike the domaintld endpoint which succeeds on the same account/session; root cause not confirmed (possibly needs an entitlement beyond asd.stdapis, or a richer multi-field inventory input) - documented as a known caveat rather than treated as fully verified. No breaking changes. (v2.2.3 was a PowerShell Gallery republish/compatibility bump only, no feature changes.) v2.2.2 : documentation-only release - live-confirmed (8.8.8.8, 1.1.1.1) that the Summary API (v2/summary/<type>/<value>, wrapped by Get-OnypheSummary) does not paginate either, same as the Simple API caveat documented in v2.2.1: any -Page value returns the same first page of results, with no error or warning, and the server always reports page:1 back regardless of what was requested. No code/behavior change - Get-OnypheSummary.ps1 and the three Invoke-APISummaryOnyphe<IP,Domain,Hostname> private wrappers'' -Page doc blocks, Howto.md, docs/Get-OnypheSummary.md and en-US/use-onyphe-help.xml now carry a NOTE pointing to Search-OnypheInfo/Export-OnypheInfo for anyone who needs more than one page of results. v2.2.1 : fixes Export-OnypheDiscoveryInfo (and every Invoke-APIBulkDiscoveryOnyphe<Category> private wrapper) silently capping each OQL query line in the Discovery API at 100 results, even when far more results actually match - Onyphe truncates without any error/warning unless a size query-string parameter is supplied. Adds an optional -Size <1-10000> parameter, opt-in, default behavior unchanged (still 100 when omitted) to avoid a breaking change. Live-verified: the same query returned 100 results by default and 2791 with -Size 10000, matching the account holder''s own count from the Onyphe website (2789, small drift from new data indexed between checks). No breaking changes since v2.2.0. v2.2.0 : adds Get-OnypheASDInfo/Get-OnypheASDAPIName, wrapping the 9 licensed "standard" ASD (Attack Surface Discovery) APIv1 endpoints (domaintld, domainwildcard, domaincertso, certsodomain, certsowildcard, dnsdomainns, dnsdomainmx, dnsdomainsoa, dnsdomainexist) - BETA endpoints requiring a Griffin View/ASM Edition non-commercial licence. The advanced Pivot Query ASD API is not yet implemented (not licensed on the account used for verification, deferred until it can be live-tested). See README.md for the full list.'
